	(text "PA_BUS programmable supply (replaces PS2 CC connector U4)\nTPS54560B buck, +12V in, 5A, fsw ~400 kHz (RT = R304).\nPA_BUS = 0.8V*(1 + R301/R302 + R301/R303) - V_DAC*R301/R303  ~=  10.07V - 2.74*V_DAC\n  PA5 = DAC2 (PA_VSET), buffer ON: 0.2V -> ~9.5V ... 3.1V -> ~1.6V.  Higher DAC code = LOWER voltage.\n  PA5 floating (reset) -> ~7.9V, so PA6 (PA_EN, R306 pull-down) keeps the converter OFF until firmware\n  has set the DAC; then drive PA_EN high.\nPA7 (PA_VSENSE, ADC12_IN7) = PA_BUS * 27k/127k for readback.\nCompensation R305/C308/C309 sized for ~20 kHz crossover (current mode, FB AC gain 0.079); verify on bench.\nLCSC numbers in the LCSC field (sourced with JLCImport). L301 = SHOU HAN CYA1265-6.8UH (15A).\nInput path sized for 5A: F2 = 6A-hold 2920 PTC (BSMD2920-600-16V), Q2 = AO4407A (SO-8, 9.5mOhm)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 20.32 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "b4a9db7e-7fa3-4fab-affe-eed13def6362")
	)
